load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# The dimension of a vector space: the number of vectors in any basis, the count of independent directions, the single
# number that says how big the space is. Dimension is forced to eight in the theory: the reversibility ceiling caps it
# at eight (no normed division algebra past the octonions) and the one-substance floor lifts it to eight (the vector
# and the half-spinor have equal size only there), so the two jaws meet and the dimension is exactly eight. The form
# carries the vector space whose dimension this is.
form dimension
  link space, like vector-space
